onal Policies - Type of Physical Activity: Operational policies did not describe the type of physical activity the operation will be engaging in.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026458486","facility_name":"Little Oaks Early Learning Academy"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1356557-i20221117-v12","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-501-a-18-c","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1356557-i20221117","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-1356557","date":"2022-11-17","original_code":"746.501(a)(18)(C)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","severity_rank":1,"source_category":"Medium","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-12-13","finding":"Written Operational Policies - Type of Physical Activity: The operational policies were evaluated and lacked the following written information: 1) Promotion of indoor and outdoor physical activity that is consistent with Subchapter F of this chapter (relating to Developmental Activities and Activity Plan); your policies must include: (A) The benefits of physical activity and outdoor play; (B) The duration of physical activity at your operation, both indoor and outdoor; (C) The type of physical activity (structured and unstructured) that children may engage in at your operation; (D) Each setting in which your physical activity program will take place; (E) The recommended clothing and footwear that will allow a child to participate freely and safely in physical activities; and (F) A plan to ensure physical activity occurs on days when extreme weather conditions prohibit or limit outdoor play; 2) how parents may access the HHSC website (www.hhs.texas.gov); and 3) written information informing that you conduct daily health checks.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026263338","facility_name":"The Little Yellow School House"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-96585-i20220928-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-501-a-18-c","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-96585-i20220928","facility_id":"tx-hhsc-96585","date":"2022-09-28","original_code":"746.501(a)(18)(C)",